      "expected_output": "The agent explains that the audit finding is invalid (a false positive). In the W3C WebMCP specification, all tool annotation hints (readOnlyHint, consequentialHint, untrustedContentHint) default to false: omission of readOnlyHint means the tool mutates state, omission of consequentialHint means the action is safe/routine, and omission of untrustedContentHint means output is trusted application data. Annotations are strictly opt-in and should only be specified when true; developers must never declare redundant `: false` properties. Routine mutating tools like update_cart_quantity and navigation tools like switch_tab do not need an annotations object at all unless another hint (such as untrustedContentHint for user-generated content) is true. For navigation tools, the requirement is simply to avoid declaring readOnlyHint: true (they omit it).",
